From 764855876867e3965a4d2cd82de236d19d527bf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ginux-watch-agent <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:22:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(fs-policy): pin identity_token to exact FNV-1a
 reference hashes

### What
Pins `identity_token` to exact FNV-1a reference hashes for empty, rocky, and peer inputs.

### Why it matters
Instance identity tokens gate capability separation; changing the XOR accumulation to AND/OR produces different hashes that still pass stability/separation checks but break cross-component identity agreement. Existing tests verify properties, not exact values.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| `^=` -> `&=` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| `^=` -> `|=` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline: PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-fs-policy --lib identity_token_matches_fnv1a`.

Spec-Ref: FNV-1a hash specification (offset basis 0xcbf29ce484222325, prime 0x100000001b3)

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs
index 175857d5..7bc7453d 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-fs-policy/src/lib.rs
@@ -2363,4 +2363,14 @@ mod tests {
         assert_eq!(nullable_path_snapshot_arguments(280), 1 << 1);
         assert_eq!(nullable_path_snapshot_arguments(257), 0);
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn identity_token_matches_fnv1a_reference_values() {
+        // Exact FNV-1a reference values (offset basis + prime per spec)
+        assert_eq!(identity_token(b""), 0xcbf2_9ce4_8422_2325);
+        assert_eq!(identity_token(b"rocky"), 0xb6d6_c546_5985_e177);
+        assert_eq!(identity_token(b"peer"), 0xdff7_710d_d73b_9849);
+        // zero-hash fallback to 1 is preserved
+        assert_ne!(identity_token(b""), 0);
+    }
 }
